  "timeframe": "1H",
  "market_context": "Uptrend on EUR/USD 1-hour chart with higher highs and higher lows; price formed a valid double top pattern and broke upward, setting up a retest entry opportunity during London session.",
  "key_observation": "The analyst identified a valid double top where the lower test’s wick hit the body of the higher peak and the higher test’s body did not exceed the lower test’s wick, confirming a bullish continuation setup.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the market direction — confirmed uptrend via higher highs and higher lows on the 1H EUR/USD chart.",
    "Step 2: Wait for a valid double top formation — verified using two rules: lower test wick hits body of higher test, and higher test body does not exceed lower test wick.",
    "Step 3: Draw a horizontal line at the close of the highest candle in the double top pattern (at 0.9900 as shown in frame f017).",
    "Step 4: Wait for price to retest that line and enter long when a candle closes above the highest point of the previous candle (rejection candle).",
    "Step 5: Place stop-loss 1 ATR (12 pips) below the lowest point of the rejection candle.",
    "Step 6: Set first TP to break even at 1:2 R:R (close half position), second TP at next structure level, checking HTF for resistance zones."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "A double top in an established trend is a high-probability continuation signal when validated by strict price action rules; retest entries with ATR-based stops and confluence with HTF structure improve trade reliability.",
